\item \code{\link[=bd_digits]{bd_digits()}}: Bangla digits to English digits and back;
\item \code{\link[=bd_place]{bd_place()}}: district, division and thana (upazila) names; codes; map spellings;
\item \code{\link[=bd_address]{bd_address()}}: post code, thana, district and division from an address;
\item \code{\link[=bd_missing]{bd_missing()}}: missing-value markers ("N/A", "-", "#N/A") to \code{NA};
\item \code{\link[=bd_squish]{bd_squish()}}: extra and invisible spaces;
\item \code{\link[=bd_check]{bd_check()}}: how many values of each column can be read, and why not;
\item \code{\link[=bd_clean]{bd_clean()}}: clean many columns of a data frame at once.
}

Data sets: \link{bd_districts}, \link{bd_divisions}, \link{bd_thanas},
\link{bd_postcodes}, \link{bd_phone_prefixes}, \link{bd_na_words}.

All functions work offline and need only base R. Tables are returned as
tibbles when the tibble package is installed.
